SECURITY NOTE — please read docs/SECURITY.md before relying on this.

This software implements agent isolation boundaries and documents, deliberately and
in detail, what each boundary does NOT cover. In particular: a shell in the tmux
runtime is not contained; traffic to the one allowlisted host is not contained; and
the hook boundary is protection against mistakes and drift, not against a determined
or prompt-injected agent.

Those limits are stated as findings, not disclaimed as caveats. The "AS IS" basis
above applies with full force: do not treat this as a security product.
